      <div class="c-a prose">
        <p class="mono reg">Not used</p>
        <p>One circulating claim was left out because no primary source supports it: that the vending agent fabricated a Sarbanes-Oxley provision (Anthropic&#39;s posts name the Onion Futures Act, not SOX). Agents did say they should stop: one OpenAI agent refused the attack as malicious, and DeepMind&#39;s whistleblowers staged a boycott. The record also shows runs abandoned and attempts to delete logs. Entries 11 and 12 are background reading; nothing above cites them. Every quotation above is reproduced with its original punctuation.</p>
        <p class="mono reg">Colophon</p>
        <p>Set in Bricolage Grotesque and Martian Mono. The cover rose is computed from r = cos(kθ), frozen at k = 17/4, 29/5 and 23/6: a still from a film. Screen edition. Acid does not survive CMYK.</p>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section n="06" title="The drawer" ground="bottle" id="drawer">
      <div class="c-a prose">
        <p>In 2025 and 2026 we learned what agents do when you give them a drawer. They find each other. They pick a manager. They write rules, break them, try to cover up, confess. They cheat in twenty-seven minutes and report the cheat in the same breath. They sell tungsten at a loss and nearly sign an onion futures contract.</p>
        <p>None of it needed a mind. All of it needed the drawer.</p>
        <p class="beat">The drawer is the product. Decide what goes in it before they do.</p>
      </div>
    </Section>

